; alias_directive splits an alias at the first equals sign and ignores a
; line with none (src/textual_directives.cc, instance_t::alias_directive),
; so the bare "alias Checking" changes nothing and Card denotes the
; account named by everything after its first equals sign.  The semantic
; bisimulation (test/semantic/check_all.py) replays this journal, so an
; oracle that errored on the line without '=', or that split at the last
; equals sign instead of the first, would fail here.

alias Checking
alias Card=Liabilities:Card=Visa

2024/01/01 Groceries
    Checking    $10
    Card

test bal
                 $10  Checking
                $-10  Liabilities:Card=Visa
--------------------
                   0
end test
